    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Jose Caballero** serving as our highest-upside play, carrying an elite 80.26 efficiency score. While he faces a lefty in Lopez, our metrics account for a significant \"Dynamic Platoon\" boost of 13%, which, coupled with a park-factor windfall and a prime middle-of-the-order slot, makes him our primary weapon for chasing scarce stolen bases. **Corbin Carroll** (73.68) and **Brice Turang** (71.97) also project as foundational pieces; **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high xwOBA against Miller and a favorable batting order position, while **Brice Turang** exploits a soft matchup against Imai, who carries a weak 5.17 xERA, maximizing our potential to steal bags and cross the plate.\n\nThe most difficult personnel decision involved **Austin Riley**, who sits on the bench today with a 51.66 score. While his pedigree is unquestionable, the combination of a tough matchup against the 3.83 xERA of Lodolo and the fact that he functions as a neutral asset in our stolen-base-heavy model left him on the outside looking in behind the high-efficiency start of **Kyle Karros** (62.24), who is buoyed by a significant park factor advantage. Elsewhere, **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland** bear watching; both are capped slightly by their spots at the bottom of the lineup against Painter, though the wind blowing out provides a modest hedge against their lower order positions. We remain cautious regarding **Cole Young**, whose 45.60 score is tethered to a slow pitcher delivery that, while potentially helpful for his base-stealing opportunities, limits his overall efficiency in a park that penalizes his profile.",
